# Training artefacts. The cache is ~200 MB of upstream CSVs and is reproducible
# from `python -m ml.sources`, so it stays out.
#
# The *reports* are checked in, because they are the evidence for the numbers in
# PRDs/ml-methodology.md and a claim without its receipt is just a claim.
#
# The *model* is checked in too, and was not. It is a build output, but nothing
# on the server builds it: Heroku installs requirements and serves, so an
# ignored artifact is an artifact production never had. The engine picker has
# been offering a model that was not there — /api/engines answered "No trained
# model artifact on this server" the whole time. 1.5 MB, and the retrain gate
# means it only changes when it is actually better.
ml/_data/
ml/artifacts/*
!ml/artifacts/xpts_model.joblib
!ml/artifacts/xpts_model.json
!ml/reports/
# Flutter build output is committed so Heroku can serve it.
# Regenerate locally with: bash scripts/deploy_flutter.sh
# flutter_web/
# Runtime log from scripts/refresh-research.sh
scripts/research.log

# Runtime log from scripts/refresh-model.sh
scripts/model.log
